  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tarte flambee is an Alsatian flatbread that bakes in minutes in a very hot oven. The base is spread with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "creme fraiche ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "creme-fraiche"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", then topped with onion sliced so thin it will "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "caramelise",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "caramelise"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in the oven and lardons that crisp at the edges. Eat it straight from the tray."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Preheat your baking tray in the oven before loading the dough. A cold tray gives a soggy base."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sea-salt-fine",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "extra-virgin-olive-oil",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "creme-fraiche",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "onion",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "large",
              "prepNote": "very thinly sliced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lardons",
              "amount": 150,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "thyme",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "sprigs",
              "prepNote": "leaves only",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "peppercorns-black",
              "amount": 0,
              "unit": "to taste",
              "prepNote": "coarsely ground",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix flour, salt, olive oil, and about 150ml water to form a smooth dough. Knead for 5 minutes. Rest for 20 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oven to its highest setting. Place a baking tray inside to heat up."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fry lardons in a dry pan until just starting to colour. Remove and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Roll dough into two very thin rounds, as thin as you can manage."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the hot tray from the oven. Lay one dough round on it."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spread generously with creme fraiche."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Top with sliced onion and lardons. Season with pepper and thyme leaves."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bake for 10 to 12 minutes until the edges are golden and crisp. Repeat with the second round."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Base is soggy",
              "cause": "Tray not preheated or cream layer too thick",
              "fix": "Preheat the tray and use a thin, even layer of creme fraiche."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Dough tears when rolling",
              "cause": "Too elastic, not rested enough",
              "fix": "Rest the dough for another 10 minutes then try again."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Onion still raw",
              "cause": "Sliced too thick or oven not hot enough",
              "fix": "Slice onion very thin and use the highest oven temperature."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tarte flambee comes from the Alsace region on the French-German border. Bakers originally used the flatbread to test the temperature of wood-fired ovens. If the tarte browned in under 2 minutes, the oven was ready for bread. The dish is now the region's most famous street food. It is eaten by hand, often at wine harvest festivals in October."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}